;; spec:   stdlib §2.5 ("about n/32 allocations"), §8.1 item 5 ("a bulk `vec` of n allocates at most n/32 + c")
;; expect: accept
;; result: 10240
;; audit:  clean
;; allocs: <= 344
;; roots:  ../../lib support
;; open:   C5
;; The page's bound, n/32 + c, with c the 24 objects of vec-from-array's constants: 320 + 24 = 344. It fails
;; today (678 objects, 664 for vec-from-array): a leaf is two objects, its array and the `VLeaf` node that holds
;; it, so the builder cannot go below n/16 + c while an enum with one field is a heap object. C5 (unboxed
;; small enums and structs by value) is the item that would remove the node; no run shows that it would, so
;; this case is open for it and nothing more is claimed. The page's n/32 is a figure of the design record that was
;; never measured (its [H] mark), and the loose cases 490 to 492 carry n/16 + 64, which the builder meets.
;; The day the count falls under the bound this case passes, which the harness reports as a failure:
;; remove `open`.
(ns main (:use fib.core fib.seq fib.coll))

(defun main () -> i64
  (let ((v (vec (array 10240 0))))
    (count v)))
